      {
        "id": 29561,
        "name": "Matchstickman",
        "username": "Matchstickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-05-03T12:47:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>No.</p>\n<p>Sonic Vortex is essentially saying “Choose up to X targets, inflict 3 sonic damage on the targets” in a single sentence, it is not multiple lines of “Chose a target, inflict 3 damage on that target”, once something has been chosen as a target for a power it is no longer a valid target for that same sentence of a card/power.</p>\n<p>A (theoretical) power that allowed you to hit the same target more than once would read “Invincible Jones deals a target 2 lightning damage.  Invincible jones deals a target 2 infernal damage” because it’s not specifying a <span class=\"bbcode-i\">second</span> target and it’s two separate sentences.</p>\n<p>(Related thread with answer from the designers <a href=\"http://greaterthangames.info/forum/index.php/topic,322.0.html\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Here</a>)</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:03:31.915Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 5719,
        "topic_slug": "sonic-vortex-question",
        "display_username": "Matchstickman",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
        "flair_bg_color": "",
        "flair_color": "",
        "flair_group_id": 41,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "link_counts": [
          {
            "url": "http://greaterthangames.info/forum/index.php/topic,322.0.html",
            "internal": false,
            "reflection": false,
            "clicks": 0
          }
        ],
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "No.\n\nSonic Vortex is essentially saying \"Choose up to X targets, inflict 3 sonic damage on the targets\" in a single sentence, it is not multiple lines of \"Chose a target, inflict 3 damage on that target\", once something has been chosen as a target for a power it is no longer a valid target for that same sentence of a card/power.\n\nA (theoretical) power that allowed you to hit the same target more than once would read \"Invincible Jones deals a target 2 lightning damage.  Invincible jones deals a target 2 infernal damage\" because it's not specifying a [i]second[/i] target and it's two separate sentences.\n\n(Related thread with answer from the designers [url=http://greaterthangames.info/forum/index.php/topic,322.0.html]Here[/url])",
